#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179452 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "db8e7d68-5731-5a44-b86e-919a13689540" :knowledge-point/title "Writing an Upper Riemann Sum for a Strictly Increasing Function"}] :question/id #uuid "b1f5f31f-55d0-5523-8225-03db04d35cb1" :question/math-academy-id "e-6248" :question/problem "Let $R = [0,2]\\times [1,3]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y) = x+2y.$ Further, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}},\\,{P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWrite down the upper Riemann sum $U(f, P).$" :question/worked-solution "The upper Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $M_{ij}$ is the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion $R_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion $R_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between $x_{i-1}$ and $x_i$ over the $x$-axis and $y_{i-1}$ and $y_i$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072435/assets/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that\n\n- $f(x,y) = x+2y$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y) = x+2y$ increases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072435/assets/67daa328cc6ae4cb37be386c327fb4548844fad2adc10476bdf1147c5a5d4218.png)\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top right corner* of each subregion. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072435/assets/6e58954fccd74eaf67c95df818c4c9050c35b324c5fffe4902a366cb295b8845.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i},{y}_{j})={x}_{i}+2{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\leq i\\leq m$ and $1\\leq j\\leq n.$\n\nFinally, the upper Riemann sum is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i}+2{y}_{j})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179453 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a5c07033-ef84-52e6-bd08-b1f0cc289e9f" :knowledge-point/title "Writing an Upper Riemann Sum for a Strictly Decreasing Function"}] :question/id #uuid "7215d75e-c001-5c28-a5e7-08a74f6543d7" :question/math-academy-id "e-6250" :question/problem "Let $R = [0,1] \\times [0,2]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y) = 90-x^2-y^2.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}},\\,{P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWrite down the upper Riemann sum $U(f, P).$" :question/worked-solution "The upper Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $M_{ij}$ is the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion $R_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion $R_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between $x_{i-1}$ and $x_i$ over the $x$-axis and $y_{i-1}$ and $y_i$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072435/assets/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that\n\n- $f(x,y) = 90-x^2-y^2$ decreases as $x$ increases on $[0,1],$ and\n\n- $f(x,y) = 90-x^2-y^2$ decreases as $y$ increases on $[0,2].$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072435/assets/ce0d90127e1f14654f4b32a933f1eb6e76e054c03f19ca40c3f04116aa3c2c93.png)\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom left corner* of each subregion. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072435/assets/5b9967c814e46914e0409854de0960e85339adc9b9fd9693677c8e048c342702.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i-1},{y}_{j-1})=90-{x}_{i-1}^{2}-{y}_{j-1}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\leq i\\leq m$ and $1\\leq j\\leq n.$\n\nFinally, the upper Riemann sum is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(90-{x}_{i-1}^{2}-{y}_{j-1}^{2})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179519 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b815d42d-8e8a-5036-b6c4-76e4c20b20b7" :knowledge-point/title "Writing an Upper Riemann Sum for a Function That’s Neither Strictly Increasing nor Decreasing"}] :question/id #uuid "79b4e8e3-5cfd-5b28-ba19-f69d2c9e0c71" :question/math-academy-id "e-9495" :question/problem "Let $R = [2,4] \\times [0,1]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y) = 2x - y.$ Further, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}},\\,{P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWrite down the upper Riemann sum $U(f,P).$" :question/worked-solution "The upper Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $M_{ij}$ is the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion $R_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion $R_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between $x_{i-1}$ and $x_i$ over the $x$-axis and $y_{i-1}$ and $y_i$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072435/assets/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that\n\n- $f(x,y) = 2x - y$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y) = 2x - y$ decreases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072435/assets/01b291ca7cd81b88cf6ed06fdcdb2ffcbb1f78255d0f57d496823d347c2fb0b3.png)\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom right corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072435/assets/de36b521dea1f925754a9c630c3d4a2c405c087a191138f1eaaa5771becb8c21.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i},{y}_{j-1})=2{x}_{i}-{y}_{j-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\leq i\\leq m$ and $1\\leq j\\leq n.$\n\nFinally, the upper Riemann sum is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(2{x}_{i}-{y}_{j-1})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186377151 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b815d42d-8e8a-5036-b6c4-76e4c20b20b7" :knowledge-point/title "Writing an Upper Riemann Sum for a Function That’s Neither Strictly Increasing nor Decreasing"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "63cb2fe1-e436-597f-a967-1e56e000c1a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7{x}_{i}-11{y}_{j-1}+5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377153} {:answer/id #uuid "a4572ffa-4a96-506d-a389-0baed3bb4b8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7{x}_{i}-11{y}_{j}+5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377154} {:answer/id #uuid "faa60f19-3e8a-54a6-917c-e8900c840487" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5{x}_{i}-{y}_{j-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377155} {:answer/id #uuid "87fe8524-60b5-584e-8e69-b704cdda4e79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7{x}_{i-1}-11{y}_{j}+5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377156} {:answer/id #uuid "42cf3831-3b4f-5ddd-9bd6-7729b78b88c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5{x}_{i-1}-{y}_{j}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377157}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "63cb2fe1-e436-597f-a967-1e56e000c1a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7{x}_{i}-11{y}_{j-1}+5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377153} :answer-field/id #uuid "7c6e8ca4-b972-571b-94cc-b42cff70ba66" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377152}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "50ce4a6a-5516-555b-90cf-b7818f652aa2" :question/math-academy-id "q-122841" :question/problem "Let $R=[-2,2]\\times [-5,-1]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=7x-11y+5.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}},\\,{P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the upper Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n\n$$\nU(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhere $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$\nwhat is the missing expression in the double summation above?" :question/worked-solution "The upper Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${M}_{ij}$ is the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion ${R}_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$ over the $x$-axis and ${y}_{i-1}$ and ${y}_{i}$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072435/assets/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x,y)=7x-11y+5$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=7x-11y+5$ decreases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072435/assets/01b291ca7cd81b88cf6ed06fdcdb2ffcbb1f78255d0f57d496823d347c2fb0b3.png)\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom right corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072435/assets/de36b521dea1f925754a9c630c3d4a2c405c087a191138f1eaaa5771becb8c21.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i},{y}_{j-1})=7{x}_{i}-11{y}_{j-1}+5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\le i\\le m$ and $1\\le j\\le n.$\n\nFinally, the upper Riemann sum is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(7{x}_{i}-11{y}_{j-1}+5)Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is $7{x}_{i}-11{y}_{j-1}+5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186377158 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b815d42d-8e8a-5036-b6c4-76e4c20b20b7" :knowledge-point/title "Writing an Upper Riemann Sum for a Function That’s Neither Strictly Increasing nor Decreasing"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "291ba459-ca01-5fb4-86bc-c4fc16e13a63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{y}_{j-1}-{x}_{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377160} {:answer/id #uuid "658fab8d-3801-5d52-975d-56a6a7bc819d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5{y}_{j}-{x}_{i-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377161} {:answer/id #uuid "9e21a3d8-1f4a-5a0a-bf77-c4c02426f064" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{y}_{j}-{x}_{i-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377162} {:answer/id #uuid "39c2b423-6bfb-5c1a-a22b-022bc9008990" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5{y}_{j}-{x}_{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377163} {:answer/id #uuid "01b41f70-fa08-505b-91db-58b3bbffa7c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5{y}_{j-1}-{x}_{i-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377164}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "658fab8d-3801-5d52-975d-56a6a7bc819d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5{y}_{j}-{x}_{i-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377161} :answer-field/id #uuid "0c2509ec-d670-5b5a-b6a8-6b1b7201de06" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377159}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "5b270f8d-0470-5a2f-bfc6-f8db0e94268e" :question/math-academy-id "q-123589" :question/problem "Let $R=[0,1]\\times [1,2]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=5y-x.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}},\\,{P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the upper Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n\n$$\nU(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhere $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ what is the missing expression in the double summation above?" :question/worked-solution "The upper Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${M}_{ij}$ is the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion ${R}_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$ over the $x$-axis and ${y}_{i-1}$ and ${y}_{i}$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072435/assets/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x,y)=5y-x$ decreases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=5y-x$ increases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072435/assets/ffa57d3e7fed08212f12d4b9d7c2e0a4d33a3aac71c8b8a03d1a9a7364484deb.png)\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top left corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072435/assets/74d546d91e145efea49b70af56cb472e8bbbd1417725cd7fa92a3a278cad75ea.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i-1},{y}_{j})=5{y}_{j}-{x}_{i-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\le i\\le m$ and $1\\le j\\le n.$\n\nFinally, the upper Riemann sum is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(5{y}_{j}-{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is $5{y}_{j}-{x}_{i-1}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186377165 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "db8e7d68-5731-5a44-b86e-919a13689540" :knowledge-point/title "Writing an Upper Riemann Sum for a Strictly Increasing Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c4fa2e5-3d4d-50a6-ba26-65b098acbd4c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "40{x}_{i-1}+2{y}_{j-1}-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377167} {:answer/id #uuid "e1fcd968-724f-5101-84f2-a7680ae577d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10{x}_{i}+{y}_{j-1}-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377168} {:answer/id #uuid "e5408759-63d8-5abc-8f8f-0166f573c96b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10{x}_{i-1}+{y}_{j-1}-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377169} {:answer/id #uuid "0d9fe437-bb36-5995-8f4a-976ebe49e278" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10{x}_{i}+{y}_{j}-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377170} {:answer/id #uuid "c5fb1508-a7cc-518a-9a0c-556f3ed4a6cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4(10{x}_{i}+{y}_{j}-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377171}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0d9fe437-bb36-5995-8f4a-976ebe49e278" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10{x}_{i}+{y}_{j}-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377170} :answer-field/id #uuid "bd563b99-7f29-589c-b4df-a22e07b531aa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377166}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0753cb3d-2dbf-5093-bb72-81d5bedeb8ec" :question/math-academy-id "q-170676" :question/problem "Let $R=[-2,2]\\times [0,4]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=10x+y-3.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}},\\,{P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the upper Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n\n$$\nU(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhere $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ what is the missing expression in the double summation above?" :question/worked-solution "The upper Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${M}_{ij}$ is the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion ${R}_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$ over the $x$-axis and ${y}_{i-1}$ and ${y}_{i}$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072435/assets/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x,y)=10x+y-3$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=10x+y-3$ increases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072435/assets/67daa328cc6ae4cb37be386c327fb4548844fad2adc10476bdf1147c5a5d4218.png)\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top right corner* of each subregion. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072435/assets/6e58954fccd74eaf67c95df818c4c9050c35b324c5fffe4902a366cb295b8845.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i},{y}_{j})=10{x}_{i}+{y}_{j}-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\le i\\le m$ and $1\\le j\\le n.$\n\nFinally, the upper Riemann sum is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(10{x}_{i}+{y}_{j}-3)Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is $10{x}_{i}+{y}_{j}-3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186377172 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a5c07033-ef84-52e6-bd08-b1f0cc289e9f" :knowledge-point/title "Writing an Upper Riemann Sum for a Strictly Decreasing Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "516b9ef9-36bb-56da-9003-2a162e1b3ade" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{x}_{i-1}^{2}-20{y}_{j-1}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377174} {:answer/id #uuid "4461c8f5-2116-5730-81fb-2330b0e9849d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{i}^{2}-5{y}_{j-1}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377175} {:answer/id #uuid "7186647d-4c6a-50fa-a689-53543a4ece03" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{x}_{i}^{2}-20{y}_{j}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377176} {:answer/id #uuid "756d2d7a-5d5f-58e4-87e8-4ac2284dd08a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{i}^{2}-5{y}_{j}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377177} {:answer/id #uuid "11d05f10-5b3c-58a1-bd48-dcc1f887d899" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{i-1}^{2}-5{y}_{j-1}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377178}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "11d05f10-5b3c-58a1-bd48-dcc1f887d899" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{i-1}^{2}-5{y}_{j-1}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377178} :answer-field/id #uuid "dcc2ccc5-d6d5-5d16-9e23-9fef8c506bdd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377173}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a0647978-d73d-55e8-962e-3a8c7c2019de" :question/math-academy-id "q-170682" :question/problem "Let $R=[-2,0]\\times [-2,2]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)={x}^{2}-5{y}^{3}.$ Further, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}},\\,{P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the upper Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n\n$$\nU(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhere $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ what is the missing expression in the double summation above?" :question/worked-solution "The upper Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${M}_{ij}$ is the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion ${R}_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$ over the $x$-axis and ${y}_{i-1}$ and ${y}_{i}$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072435/assets/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x,y)={x}^{2}-5{y}^{3}$ decreases as $x$ increases on $[-2,0],$ and\n\n- $f(x,y)={x}^{2}-5{y}^{3}$ decreases as $y$ increases on $[-2,2].$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072435/assets/ce0d90127e1f14654f4b32a933f1eb6e76e054c03f19ca40c3f04116aa3c2c93.png)\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom left corner* of each subregion. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072435/assets/5b9967c814e46914e0409854de0960e85339adc9b9fd9693677c8e048c342702.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i-1},{y}_{j-1})={x}_{i-1}^{2}-5{y}_{j-1}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\le i\\le m$ and $1\\le j\\le n.$\n\nFinally, the upper Riemann sum is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i-1}^{2}-5{y}_{j-1}^{3})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is ${x}_{i-1}^{2}-5{y}_{j-1}^{3}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186377179 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b815d42d-8e8a-5036-b6c4-76e4c20b20b7" :knowledge-point/title "Writing an Upper Riemann Sum for a Function That’s Neither Strictly Increasing nor Decreasing"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c766a63f-b440-5a42-b81f-1ba3ccdb77d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{i-1}+7{y}_{j-1}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377181} {:answer/id #uuid "e8001526-b1f3-5e62-b0ac-5ddb604d7185" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{x}_{i}-5{y}_{j}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377182} {:answer/id #uuid "889767ce-dff1-575b-9427-d8c7de94dfdf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{x}_{i-1}-5{y}_{j-1}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377183} {:answer/id #uuid "80ed9c60-c9d2-5f5a-819a-44b511323618" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{i}+7{y}_{j-1}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377184} {:answer/id #uuid "6b0099ad-3533-5bc6-9aa5-b7c80640798e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{x}_{i}-5{y}_{j-1}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377185}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6b0099ad-3533-5bc6-9aa5-b7c80640798e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{x}_{i}-5{y}_{j-1}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377185} :answer-field/id #uuid "e18b32be-1c68-5169-a74a-48b3709863d2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377180}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a066c4a1-78a1-508f-ac0c-43ce8957533e" :question/math-academy-id "q-170683" :question/problem "Let $R=[3,4]\\times [-2,5]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=3x-5y+1.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}},\\,{P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the upper Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n\n$$\nU(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhere $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$\nwhat is the missing expression in the double summation above?" :question/worked-solution "The upper Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${M}_{ij}$ is the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion ${R}_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$ over the $x$-axis and ${y}_{i-1}$ and ${y}_{i}$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072435/assets/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x,y)=3x-5y+1$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=3x-5y+1$ decreases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072435/assets/01b291ca7cd81b88cf6ed06fdcdb2ffcbb1f78255d0f57d496823d347c2fb0b3.png)\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom right corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072435/assets/de36b521dea1f925754a9c630c3d4a2c405c087a191138f1eaaa5771becb8c21.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i},{y}_{j-1})=3{x}_{i}-5{y}_{j-1}+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\le i\\le m$ and $1\\le j\\le n.$\n\nFinally, the upper Riemann sum is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(3{x}_{i}-5{y}_{j-1}+1)Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is $3{x}_{i}-5{y}_{j-1}+1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180206 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b815d42d-8e8a-5036-b6c4-76e4c20b20b7" :knowledge-point/title "Writing an Upper Riemann Sum for a Function That’s Neither Strictly Increasing nor Decreasing"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ac7ff5cd-1258-5598-8e0d-576a88b0b32f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x_{i} - 3y_{j - 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186179112} {:answer/id #uuid "ec16f68a-15b3-57fd-9e91-1bc994e24bd6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x_{i} - 3y_{j}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186179113} {:answer/id #uuid "17b225a6-859b-52c0-9d8d-26c63bbf63df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x_{i - 1} + 5y_{j}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186179114} {:answer/id #uuid "1dd95062-d1f0-5d0b-9474-d4d7354c5d76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x_{i - 1} + 5y_{j - 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186179115} {:answer/id #uuid "2f7c5167-dd2b-54f9-a925-4bc5d01e39f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x_{i - 1} - 3y_{j - 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186179116}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ac7ff5cd-1258-5598-8e0d-576a88b0b32f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x_{i} - 3y_{j - 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186179112} :answer-field/id #uuid "a8297de0-fe4c-58ea-8ed9-818e7c1ce138" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186179111}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8a3bcd08-2d96-5714-8501-bedb2f0a1010" :question/math-academy-id "q-75056" :question/problem "Let $R=[15,20]\\times [3,5]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=x-3y.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}},\\,{P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the upper Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n\n$$\nU(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhere $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$\nwhat is the missing expression in the double summation above?" :question/worked-solution "The upper Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${M}_{ij}$ is the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion ${R}_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$ over the $x$-axis and ${y}_{i-1}$ and ${y}_{i}$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072435/assets/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x,y)=x-3y$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=x-3y$ decreases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072435/assets/01b291ca7cd81b88cf6ed06fdcdb2ffcbb1f78255d0f57d496823d347c2fb0b3.png)\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom right corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072435/assets/de36b521dea1f925754a9c630c3d4a2c405c087a191138f1eaaa5771becb8c21.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i},{y}_{j-1})={x}_{i}-3{y}_{j-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\le i\\le m$ and $1\\le j\\le n.$\n\nFinally, the upper Riemann sum is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-3{y}_{j-1})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is ${x}_{i}-3{y}_{j-1}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180207 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b815d42d-8e8a-5036-b6c4-76e4c20b20b7" :knowledge-point/title "Writing an Upper Riemann Sum for a Function That’s Neither Strictly Increasing nor Decreasing"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bc2f39ec-aed9-54b6-802c-d5e9e6f78b9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y_{j} - 3x_{i - 1} + 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186179118} {:answer/id #uuid "c856dcf9-0ef2-55dd-a999-ae2cf061238c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y_{j - 1} - x_{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186179119} {:answer/id #uuid "0ad25943-af7c-5298-a2ee-e164c5ae1123" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y_{j - 1} - 3x_{i - 1} + 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186179120} {:answer/id #uuid "29b34eca-e246-50a1-bea1-4db6a2339d11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y_{j} - x_{i - 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186179121} {:answer/id #uuid "6961846c-3282-5a69-9cb4-34d864aeefc2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3y_{j} - x_{i - 1} + 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186179122}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bc2f39ec-aed9-54b6-802c-d5e9e6f78b9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y_{j} - 3x_{i - 1} + 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186179118} :answer-field/id #uuid "65af24b5-79aa-5276-b1f9-ef714e56f848" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186179117}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "42c305a2-4b3e-513e-a39c-d43ad646b48c" :question/math-academy-id "q-75060" :question/problem "Let $R=[-3,2]\\times [4,7]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=y-3x+2.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}},\\,{P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the upper Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n\n$$\nU(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhere $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ what is the missing expression in the double summation above?" :question/worked-solution "The upper Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${M}_{ij}$ is the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion ${R}_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$ over the $x$-axis and ${y}_{i-1}$ and ${y}_{i}$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072435/assets/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x,y)=y-3x+2$ decreases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=y-3x+2$ increases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072435/assets/ffa57d3e7fed08212f12d4b9d7c2e0a4d33a3aac71c8b8a03d1a9a7364484deb.png)\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top left corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072435/assets/74d546d91e145efea49b70af56cb472e8bbbd1417725cd7fa92a3a278cad75ea.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i-1},{y}_{j})={y}_{j}-3{x}_{i-1}+2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\le i\\le m$ and $1\\le j\\le n.$\n\nFinally, the upper Riemann sum is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j}-3{x}_{i-1}+2)Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is ${y}_{j}-3{x}_{i-1}+2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180209 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "db8e7d68-5731-5a44-b86e-919a13689540" :knowledge-point/title "Writing an Upper Riemann Sum for a Strictly Increasing Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8523ce4c-36f6-524a-844c-7b0a0e368281" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x_{i - 1} + y_{j} + 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186179130} {:answer/id #uuid "db41d725-0443-5c33-b8a2-2ad8c4ab19c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x_{i} + y_{j} + 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186179131} {:answer/id #uuid "f0ed8cef-370e-59c1-9dca-708699c63cb0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x_{i - 1} + y_{j - 1} + 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186179132} {:answer/id #uuid "09b927c0-fb70-5fa3-88e8-14112870e704" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x_{i} + y_{j - 1} + 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186179133} {:answer/id #uuid "6c1184ec-cd5b-5ad6-87b3-6d59d857a87d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x_{i} + y_{j}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186179134}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "db41d725-0443-5c33-b8a2-2ad8c4ab19c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x_{i} + y_{j} + 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186179131} :answer-field/id #uuid "f6c3a9a3-c355-5415-b7dc-2c22587a8580" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186179129}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f2d4f59c-ab6a-5d9c-b80f-8cb36c0c7036" :question/math-academy-id "q-75065" :question/problem "Let $R=[2,4]\\times [2,4]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=2x+y+1.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}},\\,{P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the upper Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n\n$$\nU(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhere $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ what is the missing expression in the double summation above?" :question/worked-solution "The upper Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${M}_{ij}$ is the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion ${R}_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$ over the $x$-axis and ${y}_{i-1}$ and ${y}_{i}$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072435/assets/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x,y)=2x+y+1$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=2x+y+1$ increases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072435/assets/67daa328cc6ae4cb37be386c327fb4548844fad2adc10476bdf1147c5a5d4218.png)\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top right corner* of each subregion. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072435/assets/6e58954fccd74eaf67c95df818c4c9050c35b324c5fffe4902a366cb295b8845.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i},{y}_{j})=2{x}_{i}+{y}_{j}+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\le i\\le m$ and $1\\le j\\le n.$\n\nFinally, the upper Riemann sum is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(2{x}_{i}+{y}_{j}+1)Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is $2{x}_{i}+{y}_{j}+1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186377186 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "db8e7d68-5731-5a44-b86e-919a13689540" :knowledge-point/title "Writing an Upper Riemann Sum for a Strictly Increasing Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a8e8d495-76d3-5c63-adb3-9eeb0ede4bfe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{i}+5{y}_{j}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377188} {:answer/id #uuid "f56dc597-c9fb-5d99-9e53-72b47e238fe2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{i-1}+5{y}_{j-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377189} {:answer/id #uuid "47262f29-7516-5b4f-818e-cc8a44e656bd" :