tition. This subregion lies between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$ over the $x$-axis and ${y}_{i-1}$ and ${y}_{i}$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072435/assets/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x,y)=11{x}^{2}+13{y}^{2}-9$ increases as $x$ increases on $[1,7],$ and\n\n- $f(x,y)=11{x}^{2}+13{y}^{2}-9$ increases as $y$ increases on $[3,5].$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072435/assets/67daa328cc6ae4cb37be386c327fb4548844fad2adc10476bdf1147c5a5d4218.png)\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top right corner* of each subregion. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072435/assets/6e58954fccd74eaf67c95df818c4c9050c35b324c5fffe4902a366cb295b8845.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i},{y}_{j})=11{x}_{i}^{2}+13{y}_{j}^{2}-9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\le i\\le m$ and $1\\le j\\le n.$\n\nFinally, the upper Riemann sum is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(11{x}_{i}^{2}+13{y}_{j}^{2}-9)Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is $11{x}_{i}^{2}+13{y}_{j}^{2}-9.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186377207 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a5c07033-ef84-52e6-bd08-b1f0cc289e9f" :knowledge-point/title "Writing an Upper Riemann Sum for a Strictly Decreasing Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "447b11db-5a42-5c11-8d32-df2822c95231" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "17-{x}_{i}-4{y}_{j-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377209} {:answer/id #uuid "7908c932-7258-5704-b6d4-6ad4170dcb80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6{x}_{i-1}-{y}_{j-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377210} {:answer/id #uuid "159f5b22-268d-5c8b-aaa2-bb45ca9d921e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "17-{x}_{i-1}-4{y}_{j-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377211} {:answer/id #uuid "a44f3740-83bf-55e9-812f-7e8d2452d26d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "17-{x}_{i-1}-4{y}_{j}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377212} {:answer/id #uuid "10f79fe9-d105-5614-965a-3632732ac87a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6{x}_{i-1}-{y}_{j}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377213}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "159f5b22-268d-5c8b-aaa2-bb45ca9d921e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "17-{x}_{i-1}-4{y}_{j-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377211} :answer-field/id #uuid "af40acf8-a1d3-5ffd-96f9-e6c543d5c6af" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377208}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2e2cd5a2-fcda-50ad-85fe-18993ba6ce93" :question/math-academy-id "q-75338" :question/problem "Let $R=[-8,-3]\\times [-6,-1]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=17-x-4y.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}},\\,{P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the upper Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n\n$$\nU(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhere $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ what is the missing expression in the double summation above?" :question/worked-solution "The upper Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${M}_{ij}$ is the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion ${R}_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$ over the $x$-axis and ${y}_{i-1}$ and ${y}_{i}$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072435/assets/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x,y)=17-x-4y$ decreases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=17-x-4y$ decreases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072435/assets/ce0d90127e1f14654f4b32a933f1eb6e76e054c03f19ca40c3f04116aa3c2c93.png)\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom left corner* of each subregion. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072435/assets/5b9967c814e46914e0409854de0960e85339adc9b9fd9693677c8e048c342702.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i-1},{y}_{j-1})=17-{x}_{i-1}-4{y}_{j-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\le i\\le m$ and $1\\le j\\le n.$\n\nFinally, the upper Riemann sum is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(17-{x}_{i-1}-4{y}_{j-1})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is $17-{x}_{i-1}-4{y}_{j-1}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186377214 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a5c07033-ef84-52e6-bd08-b1f0cc289e9f" :knowledge-point/title "Writing an Upper Riemann Sum for a Strictly Decreasing Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "91966aeb-0775-5045-add8-a88656c88062" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "35-3{x}_{i-1}-9{y}_{j}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377216} {:answer/id #uuid "d74cbaa9-abfc-533c-a5b2-b4dea1396cdc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "35-3{x}_{i}-9{y}_{j-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377217} {:answer/id #uuid "b531c311-e921-500e-be8e-82feb508d9fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}_{i-1}+3{y}_{j-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377218} {:answer/id #uuid "e5dbaddb-5dd4-5c8c-9df9-30600b226deb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}_{i}+3{y}_{j-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377219} {:answer/id #uuid "37914056-659b-5819-b8c5-52ec453bbf0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "35-3{x}_{i-1}-9{y}_{j-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377220}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "37914056-659b-5819-b8c5-52ec453bbf0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "35-3{x}_{i-1}-9{y}_{j-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377220} :answer-field/id #uuid "3a6128d1-d3b2-5dce-bb50-5482aa564407" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377215}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "06dfd563-822d-52e7-b52e-e47d3c7d2022" :question/math-academy-id "q-75339" :question/problem "Let $R=[-5,2]\\times [2,3]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=35-3x-9y.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}},\\,{P}_{2}={{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the upper Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n\n$$\nU(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhere $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ what is the missing expression in the double summation above?" :question/worked-solution "The upper Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${M}_{ij}$ is the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion ${R}_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$ over the $x$-axis and ${y}_{i-1}$ and ${y}_{i}$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072435/assets/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x,y)=35-3x-9y$ decreases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=35-3x-9y$ decreases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072435/assets/ce0d90127e1f14654f4b32a933f1eb6e76e054c03f19ca40c3f04116aa3c2c93.png)\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom left corner* of each subregion. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072435/assets/5b9967c814e46914e0409854de0960e85339adc9b9fd9693677c8e048c342702.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i-1},{y}_{j-1})=35-3{x}_{i-1}-9{y}_{j-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\le i\\le m$ and $1\\le j\\le n.$\n\nFinally, the upper Riemann sum is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(35-3{x}_{i-1}-9{y}_{j-1})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is $35-3{x}_{i-1}-9{y}_{j-1}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186377221 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a5c07033-ef84-52e6-bd08-b1f0cc289e9f" :knowledge-point/title "Writing an Upper Riemann Sum for a Strictly Decreasing Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17e0f50c-7c94-57ea-8af6-121ca782dc9d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "135-4{x}_{i-1}^{2}-13{y}_{j-1}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 175921